design:
GOAL: after any ranked game, Home's card (ratings per type, league, level/XP bar, games/win%/streak), Modes, GameType ("הדירוג שלך") and the surrender estimate show the new numbers without a restart. The server stays authoritative. Nothing changes on the server or in the protocol.

1) CONFIG: apps/mobile/src/config/account.ts. Add to accountConfig:
  refresh: {
    /** Home's focus and the app's return to the foreground read GET /v1/me at most this often (ms). */
    minIntervalMs: 30_000,
    afterRanked: {
      /** Waits before each read of GET /v1/me after a ranked game ends, until the server has stored it (ms). */
      confirmDelaysMs: [1500, 3000, 6000, 12000, 24000],
      /** A rated game that moved no rating of mine (no RatingChange for me): read me + progress at these waits, nothing to confirm. */
      unratedDelaysMs: [1500, 6000],
      /** How long the game's own rating change is shown over older server answers (ms). After that, the server's answer wins. */
      optimisticTtlMs: 120_000,
      /** Leaving a running 2-player ranked game: the first read waits rules.graceMs plus this (ms). */
      afterGraceMarginMs: 2000,
    },
  }
These are tunables, not literals in code.

2) PURE HELPERS: apps/mobile/src/api/me.ts (no RN; tests in api/__tests__/accountApi.test.ts):
  - `ratingEntryAfter(entry: RatingEntry, after: number, gamesBefore: number, provisionalGames: number): RatingEntry`.
    Returns the entry as ratings/store.ts applyRatingChanges will store it: { key: entry.key, rating: after, games: gamesBefore + 1, provisional: gamesBefore + 1 < provisionalGames, peak: Math.max(entry.peak, after) }.
    Do NOT use RatingChange.provisional. It means "K doubled in this game", which is a different flag.
  - `withRatingEntry(me: Me, entry: RatingEntry): Me`. Replaces the entry with the same key. If no entry has that key, returns the same object; never invents keys.
  - `export interface PendingRating { meId: string; entry: RatingEntry; expiresAt: number }`
  - `withPendingRatings(server: Me, pending: ReadonlyMap<string, PendingRating>, now: number): { me: Me; pending: Map<string, PendingRating> }`.
    A pending entry is kept (and shown in place of the server's entry for its key) only when all of these hold:
      - p.meId === server.id;
      - p.expiresAt > now;
      - the server has that key;
      - server entry.games < p.entry.games.
    Otherwise it is dropped (the server confirmed it, it expired, or another account). The returned `pending` holds only the kept ones.

3) NEW apps/mobile/src/game/rankedEnd.ts (pure; imports engine ratingKey and types only):
  export interface RankedEnd {
    gameId: string;
    playerId: PlayerId;          // my id in the game = users.id = Me.id in ranked games
    key: string;                 // ratingKey(config.gameType, config.players.length, config.rules.rating.option), as the server's fake client does
    gamesBefore: number;         // config.players[me].ratedGames ?? 0 (the server's count at the start)
    provisionalGames: number;    // config.rules.rating.provisionalGames
    change: RatingChange | null; // mine from state.result.ratingChanges, else null
    expectsStored: boolean;      // the server will add 1 to games in `key` for me
    waitMs: number;              // extra wait before the first read
  }
  - `rankedEndOf(state: GameState, me: PlayerId): RankedEnd | null`.
    Returns null unless ALL of these hold:
      - state.status === 'over' and state.result exists;
      - config.mode === 'ranked';
      - config.players.length >= 2;
      - every player has rating !== undefined (a rated room; dev rooms have none, and nothing is stored);
      - me is one of the players.
    Then change = mine ?? null, expectsStored = change !== null, waitMs = 0.
  - `rankedLeftOf(state: GameState, me: PlayerId, marginMs: number): RankedEnd | null`.
    For a rated game that is NOT over and has exactly 2 players: change null, expectsStored true, waitMs = config.rules.graceMs + marginMs.
    Returns null for 3–4 players: their game ends (and is stored) only when the whole game ends, so Home's focus and the foreground cover it.
  - `storedIn(server: Me, end: RankedEnd): boolean`. True when end.expectsStored and the server's entry for end.key has games > end.gamesBefore.
  This must stay aligned with the server: applyRatingChanges increments games exactly for the players present in result.ratingChanges. The parallel items that change the retire rules will change which players get a RatingChange, and this predicate follows automatically.

4) apps/mobile/src/game/onlineSession.ts:
  - OnlineSessionDeps gets `onEnd?: (end: { state: GameState; playerId: PlayerId; left: boolean }) => void`.
  - In onUpdate, in the same `!this.ended && state.status === 'over' && state.result` branch that sends game_end, call it once with left: false, wrapped in try/catch like send().
